WEBVTT

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:11.250
Shimamura... Chocolate.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.290
Shimamura...

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:17.790
Homemade... is probably a bit heavy.
I've never cooked before, anyway.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:20.450
I'll just buy one.

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:29.750
On February 14th, I was going
to go somewhere with Shimamura

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.870
and exchange chocolates with her.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.330
Shimamura...

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:43.450
--It'll be exciting to see what Hyodo
can do with their record next week.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.870
--Anyway, I need to ask her what she likes.
--It'll be exciting to see what Hyodo
can do with their record next week.

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:47.750
--And now, the moment everyone's
been waiting for, romance horoscopes!

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:52.330
--I need to make sure I don't regret anything.
--And now, the moment everyone's
been waiting for, romance horoscopes!

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.910
This is Shaman Taoka's...

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.830
...Romance horoscopes!

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:04.750
"Shaman Taoka's Romance Horoscopes"

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:11.040
I'm here to tell you all about
your romance luck again today!

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.160
Now, then...

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:31.200
"Missed Call Just Now
Tarumi"

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.700
"Missed Call Just Now
Tarumi"

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.700
Tarumi?

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.250
I'll give you a call when I get home.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:22.790
"Libra"

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:22.790
I see some rough times ahead
for the Libras today.

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:25.290
"Libra"

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:25.290
Make sure you're aware of your surroundings!

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:28.700
Today's lucky letter is... D!

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:37.620
Adachi?

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.120
Um, what's up?

00:03:56.120 --> 00:04:00.660
Did you want something? Like milk tea or bread?

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:03.040
I'm fine.

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:07.500
Say... what's your sign, Shimamura?

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:08.750
My sign?

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:13.950
I'm not sure. I was born in April...
Oh, April 10th.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:16.700
Which means she's an Aries.

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:25.250
If she's an Aries, I think our
compatibility sucks, since I'm a Libra.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:26.830
No, that can't be true!

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:30.410
There's no way I'd want to get closer
to someone who's not compatible...

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:32.580
I don't think...

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.290
No way...

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:37.370
Adachi? Hello?

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:42.250
Why did you want to know my sign,
anyway? Are you into astrology?

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:47.450
Oh, I, uh... I need to get
ready for our next class...

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.750
Get ready? What?

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:58.580
Well, at least I managed to find out
when Shimamura's birthday is.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:00.410
"Tarumi"

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:04.330
Shimamura!

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:06.410
Shimamura, wait!

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.540
What's up, Adachi?

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:14.410
Hey, um... What kind of chocolate do you like?

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.700
Huh? Chocolate?

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:17.410
Yes, chocolate.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:22.660
Let's see... I think I'm a fan of
milk chocolate. It goes down better.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:24.290
I see.

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:25.500
Was that it?

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:26.750
Yeah.

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:29.580
Adachi?

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.790
What about your bike?

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:33.540
I forgot!

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:40.370
"Libra"

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:40.370
Bam, tap, bam, tap, bam, ow!

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:43.870
Libras...

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:49.250
Change up your hairstyle
to really grab your crush's attention.

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:52.120
Today's lucky letter is A.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.200
Oh, there you are.

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:10.000
Hey, wanna have lunch together?

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:15.080
Wait, is that all chocolate?

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:21.910
Did you, like, use your head too much
studying that you need the extra carbs?

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:25.160
Y-Yeah, I think that's it.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:26.700
Huh...

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:46.830
Hey, your ponytail's cute.
Though I like you just the way you are usually.

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:56.660
U-U... Usually?!

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:58.750
A-Adachi?

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:03.700
Hello? Your chocolate?

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:11.950
Milk chocolate, eh?

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:21.950
"Though I like you
just the way you are usually."

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:25.080
Say how you really feel today.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.660
You never know when you're gonna die.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:30.500
Die! Die! Die!

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:34.200
I became a lot more positive
after meeting Shimamura.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:37.370
Actually, I'm so positive
that I'm about to burst,

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:40.250
but my days are now brighter, nonetheless.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:43.790
That's why I want to tell her
how much I appreciate her.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:48.120
Shimamura is my sun.

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:51.500
G-Good morning.

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:53.160
Morning...

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:56.080
Did you need something?

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:01.950
No, I just, um...
wanted to talk about the sun...

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:04.040
Huh?

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:05.950
No, not that part! You wanted to show gratitude.

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:09.830
Um... Gratitude, gratitude,
how do I show gratitude?

00:08:09.830 --> 00:08:12.160
Th-Thank you...

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:14.080
Huh? Wait, what?

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:17.450
I didn't do anything to
get thanked... Wait, what?

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:20.160
So, yeah.

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:25.790
I'm not sure if I became
more positive or just stupider.

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:27.660
Libras out there,

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:30.830
make sure you hurry up and
give them your homemade chocolate.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:35.910
Do it! Your lucky letter today is C!

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:42.580
"Chocolate They'll Think Is Delicious"

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:54.500
Is this... Chocolate?

00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:59.410
"Well?"

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:01.450
"Well?"
"Well?"

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:05.250
What a pain.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:10.830
Even I'd feel awkward
if someone sent this to me.

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:15.580
I want Shimamura to be happy.
I want her to think I'm special.

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:19.830
My wishes and desires kept piling up
far and high like mountain ranges,

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:24.540
but what I was seeing before me
was an endless wasteland.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:29.750
It was better off before I messed with it.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:37.200
Hup.

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:38.830
"Tarumi
Incoming Call"

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:40.450
"Tarumi
Incoming Call"

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:40.450
Tarumi...

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:42.750
Hello?

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:44.200
Hey, Shima?

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:46.080
Yup, that's me.

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:49.450
Sorry I didn't call you back earlier.

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:53.250
No, it's fine. We haven't
talked since grade school.

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:55.450
Hey.

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:58.870
I forgot to mention this the other day.

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:00.620
What?

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:03.660
I was really happy to see you again.

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:07.120
Also... That's it.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:11.160
That's it? Happy, huh?

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:25.500
Hm... I guess I don't mind that.

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:36.620
Wow, look at that hair.

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:38.410
That's what shocks you?

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:45.330
Shimamura, let's go see a movie.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:46.160
What?

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:47.160
Let's go!

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:50.660
Why don't you two go? I've gotta study.

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:56.250
Go with them. And make sure they get some lunch.

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:58.330
--Let us go!
--Let's go!

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:12.200
I thought I spotted some teacher
with some kids, but it's Shimamu!

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:14.540
Hino... Why are you dressed like that?

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.330
Just got back from some family business.

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:18.330
Is she your friend?

00:11:18.330 --> 00:11:20.330
Yeah.

00:11:20.330 --> 00:11:23.450
Ah, Hino. It's been a while.

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:28.290
Huh? Um... Who might you be? Well, whatever.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:32.370
So I guess you've been dragging the runts
around today on a family discount.

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:34.660
We went to see a movie!

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:36.410
Hey, where's Nagafuji?

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:39.450
We don't hang out on our days off, too.

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:42.790
Though maybe I'll go buy some
chocolate on my way home.

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:44.660
Are you giving some to Nagafuji?

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:48.120
I mean, it's more like I'll give it to her
and we'll both eat it on the spot.

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:49.660
We do that every year.

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:53.620
Huh... So, why do you buy Nagafuji chocolate?

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:54.660
--Why? Because it makes Nagafuji happy?
And we both like chocolate.

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:59.580
--Spinny, spin... Spinny, spin...
--Why? Because it makes Nagafuji happy?
And we both like chocolate.

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:02.000
Huh...

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:06.200
I guess that's all there is
to a girls' Valentine's together.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:11.160
Adachi's way too eager... And she's too excited.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:18.290
Maybe we're both overthinking
Valentine's Day way too much.

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:21.620
You and your destined prince...

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:23.500
...have an exciting encounter!

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:30.830
Adachi!

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:35.040
We're gonna play some games.
Wanna go to Nagafuji's house with us?

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:36.120
Right now?

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:37.660
Yeah.

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:41.000
I don't know much about games, though...

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:44.950
I see. Well, I'm not going to twist your arm.

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:52.750
No, wait. I'll go.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.330
All right! The gang's all here!

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:57.750
Ow!

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:00.200
Are you sure?

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:01.450
Y-Yeah...

00:13:01.450 --> 00:13:05.450
"Chief Adachi: 5,000,000 yen"

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:10.160
Another six. Looks like you're off
to a great start, Adachi.

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:12.830
Guess it's my turn... now!

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:14.790
"Nagafuji Pro: 6,500,000 yen"
"Nippon Budokan"

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:16.620
"Nagafuji Pro: 6,500,000 yen"
"Nippon Budokan"

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:16.620
A two...

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:20.250
You just need to keep squishing your boobs. Hup.

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:22.790
"Mrs. Hino: 15,000,000 yen"
"Sunshine 60"

00:13:22.790 --> 00:13:26.120
Nice, nice! Hup...

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:29.330
Okay, here I go.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:37.620
What? A one? Ugh!

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:40.040
Here you go. Have some fresh croquettes.

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:42.370
Heck yeah! Love you, Auntie!

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:44.580
It sure is lively today.

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:49.040
I wonder where Hino went off to...

00:13:49.040 --> 00:13:49.870
Shuffup.

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:52.450
"Mrs. Hino: 27,000,000 yen"

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:52.450
What am I supposed to do in Hokkaido?

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:56.660
What? I got Okinawa.
The goal is Nagoya, isn't it?

00:13:56.660 --> 00:14:00.790
Let's see... Dang it, I got a one again.

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:04.160
Come on, Adachicchi.

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:06.370
You're only four spaces from the goal.

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:08.250
For real?

00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:10.370
You need a four. You've got this.

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:11.660
O-Okay...

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.160
"Chief Adachi: 52,000,000 yen"

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.370
"Nagoya Castle"

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:18.660
I got a four.

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:22.120
Aw, the first one in's Adacchi?

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:27.410
Way to go, Adachi.

00:14:27.410 --> 00:14:31.040
Wait. That means I'm in last place!

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:32.370
"Nagafuji Butcher Shop"

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:35.160
"Nagafuji Butcher Shop"

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:35.160
You were in last place until the end.

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:37.790
"Nagafuji Butcher Shop"

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:37.790
Only people with bad personalities
are good at this game,

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:40.870
so I guess you're a great person, Shimamura.

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:45.500
I do think you're a great person.

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:48.120
Thanks...

00:14:48.120 --> 00:14:49.620
We can play again some other time.

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:52.120
--Yeah.
--Be careful getting home!

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.330
Did you at least have some fun, Adachi?

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:56.700
Um... Yeah.

00:14:56.700 --> 00:15:01.000
I see. Actually, I think
I asked you this before, too.

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:04.540
U-Um, want me to give you a ride home?

00:15:04.540 --> 00:15:06.830
It'd be really out of the way. Are you sure?

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:13.500
But you know, Adachi...

00:15:13.500 --> 00:15:17.540
You seem way different from when we first met.

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:20.450
D-Don't say that.

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:22.620
Time passes by so quickly.

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:28.540
I'm just being trifled with in this
completely different flow of time.

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:31.540
Um... Shimamura.

00:15:31.540 --> 00:15:34.120
Um, in three days...

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:37.540
I haven't forgotten about the chocolate.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:38.370
Yeah!

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:41.160
Hey, Adachi! Eyes up front!

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:47.080
S-Sorry!

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:53.580
I'm pretty sure Shimamura is stealing my time.

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:58.200
But that time, unlike the
colorless days I've spent,

00:15:58.200 --> 00:16:01.790
is so filled with light, just like a jewel.

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:07.870
One, two! One, two!

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:10.450
Crap... I might not make it.

00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:16.120
One, two! One, two! One, two!

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:18.000
One, two...

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:23.120
Well, if it isn't Shimamura.

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:25.000
Did you need something?

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:31.950
Not exactly. Or rather, aren't you cold?
Look at what you're wearing.

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:34.040
Jeez, you're cold.

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:38.750
You're not going to school?

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:40.370
What are you talking about?

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:44.950
I'm a fine adult, so I don't have to go!

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:47.080
An adult, eh?

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:50.040
If you're not showing up to school at that age,

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:52.870
you're heading right down the path
to becoming a delinquent.

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:07.950
I'll have you know, Shimamura,
I'm around 680 years old.

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:09.540
Yeah, yeah.

00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:12.910
Anyway, I actually have school,
so see you later.

00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:14.330
Bye-bye.

00:17:27.830 --> 00:17:29.660
Oh, jeez...

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:34.080
This ninja art is quite useful.

00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:35.370
Ninja art?

00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:39.540
Ninja Art: Make Them Turn Around
By Staring at Them. <i>Nin, nin.</i>

00:17:39.540 --> 00:17:46.250
Ninja art, my ass. I just came back
because I'm a really good person.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:51.620
Why, yesh. You sure are
a good pershon, Shimamura.

00:17:51.620 --> 00:17:54.450
Yes. So thank me.

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:56.120
Thank you!

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:07.040
"I see, thanks"
"You're not coming today?"

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:08.910
"I see, thanks"
"Unread: You're not coming today?"

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:12.660
"Unread: You're not coming today?"

00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:17.830
If you want to get closer,
you need to make the first move.

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:19.790
You can't keep waiting forever!

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:25.330
Coming!

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:26.330
Huh?

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:33.540
Ah, I believe your name was Adachi.

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:37.410
Yeah... So, where's Shimamura?

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:39.660
Wait, what?

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:43.040
She's taking a nap.

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:43.950
Huh?!

00:18:43.950 --> 00:18:46.250
So make sure you shh! Shh!

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:47.500
Right...

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:49.750
Oh, perfect timing.

00:18:49.750 --> 00:18:54.950
I must go procure dinner soon.

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:59.330
And so, I leave this to you, you...

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:02.040
Oh. Hey, Adachi.

00:19:02.040 --> 00:19:04.120
Sh-Shimamura...

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:10.000
So where's Yashiro?

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:14.540
Um... She said something about procuring dinner.

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:16.290
She sure does whatever she wants to.

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:18.580
So what brings you here, Adachi?

00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:23.700
Huh? Well, you weren't at school today,
so I thought you maybe had a cold...

00:19:23.700 --> 00:19:25.410
I sent you a message.

00:19:25.410 --> 00:19:26.870
A message?

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:30.580
Oh, sorry. I left it in my bag.

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:32.580
So that's why I came to see how you were doing,

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:35.540
but I guess I might've woken you up.

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:42.500
You're pretty decent, Adachi.

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:54.870
Oh, sorry. I just...

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:05.250
When she looks like this,
I can tell what Adachi wants from me.

00:20:05.250 --> 00:20:08.330
Something she can lean onto that'll support her.

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:11.660
Previously, it was the gym wall.

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:17.160
But at some point, that turned into me.

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:21.330
It's not like I don't wonder about why that is,

00:20:21.330 --> 00:20:26.910
but the fact of the matter is, I am indeed
spending time with Adachi like this.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:35.580
Today's lucky letter is A!

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:39.830
This lucky letter was passed down
from my great ancestor, Himi...

00:20:39.830 --> 00:20:44.830
Hey, wait... D-Don't forget to buy chocolates!

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:51.080
Here.

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:53.200
Hiyah.

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:56.950
Oh, yeah. I need to buy chocolate today.

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:07.790
Maybe Adachi wants to go back to that place.

00:21:07.790 --> 00:21:10.700
But if we insisted on going
to that place right now,

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:16.370
we'd probably freeze
and wouldn't be able to do anything.

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:21.250
The seasons continue to change,
and we go along for the ride.

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:23.200
And I think that's fine.

00:21:24.370 --> 00:21:27.410
<i>Dandan </i>noodles and a
half order of fried rice up.

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:30.330
Sorry to call you in suddenly.

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:31.870
No, it's fine...

00:21:31.870 --> 00:21:36.160
What should I do though?
I was planning on buying chocolate today.

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:43.700
"Tarumi
Incoming Call"

00:21:44.870 --> 00:21:45.910
Hello?

00:21:45.910 --> 00:21:48.410
Oh, Shima? Sorry to call you out of the blue.

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:49.410
It's fine.

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:51.700
Um, are you free right now?

00:21:51.700 --> 00:21:53.330
Huh?

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:58.200
Chocolate... Chocolate...
Chocolate for Shimamura.

00:22:00.660 --> 00:22:02.330
Oh, right.

00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:06.540
I'm going out with Shimamura tomorrow,
so I guess I can just pick then.

00:22:06.540 --> 00:22:08.200
Wake up!

00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:09.580
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:22:16.580 --> 00:22:17.950
Tarumi.

00:22:22.160 --> 00:22:22.450
"Episode 8 'The Briar That
Weaves the Past: Old Rose'"

00:22:22.450 --> 00:22:23.910
"Episode 8 'The Briar That
Weaves the Past: Old Rose'"

00:22:22.450 --> 00:22:23.910
Heyo.

00:22:23.910 --> 00:22:25.830
"Episode 8 'The Briar That
Weaves the Past: Old Rose'"

00:22:25.830 --> 00:22:28.000
"Episode 8 'The Briar That
Weaves the Past: Old Rose'"

00:22:25.830 --> 00:22:28.000
Heya.

00:23:57.950 --> 00:24:01.040
"Next Time: 'Love That Embraces
the Holy Mother: Marigold'"

00:23:57.950 --> 00:24:01.040
Adashimapedia: Fortunetelling.

00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:03.200
"Next Time: 'Love That Embraces
the Holy Mother: Marigold'"

00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:03.200
Yes, I see it! I see your future!

00:24:03.200 --> 00:24:06.000
"Next Time: 'Love That Embraces
the Holy Mother: Marigold'"

00:24:03.200 --> 00:24:06.000
I guess you figured out
that I'm going to kiss you, then.

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:06.830
"Next Time: 'Love That Embraces
the Holy Mother: Marigold'"

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:06.830
Wait, you are?

00:24:06.830 --> 00:24:09.290
"Next Time: 'Love That Embraces
the Holy Mother: Marigold'"

00:24:06.830 --> 00:24:09.290
So, where does it say that I'm going to kiss you?

00:24:09.290 --> 00:24:11.000
"Next Time: 'Love That Embraces
the Holy Mother: Marigold'"

00:24:09.290 --> 00:24:11.000
Well... The forehead, right?

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:13.000
"Next Time: 'Love That Embraces
the Holy Mother: Marigold'"

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:13.000
Oh, I don't know about that...
